  "description": "The 20 public photos of the Depth Anything V2-Small oracle (training/depth/oracle.py, D-02; the gate of D-03, docs/13, docs/algorithms/06 section 8.6). All are JPEG files on Wikimedia Commons whose page carries a CC0 tag (seven are photos of the SAM 2 oracle, training/sam2/oracle_photos.json, with the hashes pinned there), read from Commons' API on 2026-11-07; the licence is the uploader's declaration on the page `page`, so check it there before using a photo for anything else. The oracle downloads them, checks each against `sha256` and never commits them; `commons_sha1` is Commons' own hash of the same file. A `sha256` of TBD-after-first-run means the file itself could not be downloaded when the list was written (Wikimedia's upload server was not reachable from the author's environment): the oracle then checks Commons' SHA-1 instead, prints the SHA-256 it found, keeps it as `photo_sha256` in manifest.json of the fixtures, and the value is copied here after the first run. If a file on Commons is replaced its hash changes and the oracle refuses it: pick another photo, never loosen the check. `categories` says what each photo is there to test: portrait, hair, foliage, sky, glass, interior, shallow-focus, flat (a flat picture of a flat object), and a few more. They were chosen from the files' titles and descriptions; nobody has looked at every photo yet (the contact sheets of D-06 will). `intermediates` marks the three photos whose fixtures hold every stage of the network (a landscape, a portrait and a nearly square photo); the others hold the picture, the input tensor and the depth map.",
